WEBVTT

00:03:55.648 --> 00:04:00.945
a vibrant hobby as a self-taught
and later acclaimed woodcarver;

00:04:00.987 --> 00:04:03.948
confidence in others;

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.701
a many-decades-long marriage;

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.203
a family, a home.

00:04:09.954 --> 00:04:14.375
And he had the chance to read it all
long before he died.

00:04:15.418 --> 00:04:17.712
So that had me asking,

00:04:17.712 --> 00:04:20.881
why are eulogies only for dead people?

00:04:22.675 --> 00:04:26.887
Why do we wait so long
to recognize each other's gifts?

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.976
Why are the truest compliments
and the sincerest sentiments